{% doc %}
  The gear collection's URL, resolved rather than constructed. Outputs a bare
  path and nothing else, so callers can capture it:

      {%- capture gear_url -%}{%- render 'gear-url' -%}{%- endcapture -%}

  WHY THIS IS NOT JUST A STRING. The collection is being renamed from
  swinglab-gear to gear, and the rename is a manual Shopify action that happens
  at cutover — after this theme is written and possibly after it is published.
  So there is a window in which the theme exists and the new handle does not.

  Hardcoding either handle is wrong in one half of that window, and the 301
  does not save it: Shopify creates the redirect at rename time running
  old -> new, which rescues links to the OLD handle and can never rescue a link
  to the new one written before the rename. Six unguarded
  `routes.collections_url | append: '/gear'` sites shipped that way and every
  one of them was a live 404 — including the 404 page's own "Training gear"
  escape hatch, which sent a lost visitor to another 404.

  So the handle is resolved against what the store actually has, newest first,
  and only falls back to constructing a path if neither collection is found.
  Presence is tested on `.handle`, never on the drop itself: `collections[...]`
  returns a TRUTHY drop for a handle that does not exist.

  Delete the legacy arm once the rename has been live long enough that no
  cached page still points at the old handle.
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign gear_collection = collections['gear']
  if gear_collection.handle == blank
    assign gear_collection = collections['swinglab-gear']
  endif

  if gear_collection.handle != blank
    assign resolved = gear_collection.url
  else
    assign resolved = routes.collections_url | append: '/gear'
  endif
-%}
{{- resolved -}}
